  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea™ series contains 3 PeriPro femur plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Proximal Femur (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Distal Femur**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Interprosthetic Femur**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pangea Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive locking position in the plate’s locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V ELI material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423202/images/822c9197-fca3-4dab-891d-1d8114ef915a_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_4.03.55_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Circular universal holes accept nonlocking screws, and locking screws within a 30° cone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Proximal Screw Cluster**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to offer bicortical screw fixation around a hip stem",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Oblong Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To aid in plate placement and serve as an attachment site for targeter",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Staggered Screw Pattern**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Staggered screw hole trajectories in the diaphysis are designed to accommodate screw placement in the anterior and posterior cortex around an intramedullary nail or a prosthesis.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423202/images/126fe5db-c066-4ab9-9182-c337dd29606c_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_4.04.02_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Waisted Scalloped Shape**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Cable Plug Compatible**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Cable plugs accepted in any round screw hole and may be used in conjunction with a 2.0mm vitallium cable",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Tapered End**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "For atraumatic submuscular insertion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Plate lengths range from 257mm to 371mm",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Radius of Curvature changes for longest plate length to fascilitate fit",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Maximum THA Stem Coverage: ≤100mm to 215mm",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The PeriPRO Femur Plating System is indicated for internal fixation and stabilization of femur fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone. This includes:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Fracture in the presence of intramedullary implants, including periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approaches",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Surgeons may use a standard lateral or modified lateral approach to the proximal femur.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
